# Verify Before Claim

Do not assert bare numeric claims unless a tool in the same or next turn produced that number.

## Bare counts are forbidden without tool evidence

Do not state test counts, file counts, percentages, scenario counts, or similar
quantities from memory or estimation. First run a tool (`pytest -q`,
`git status`, `rg -c`, `wc -l`, `ls`, etc.) and only then report the number the
tool printed.

## Correction language must cite the tool

If you previously stated a number and then use correction language
(`actually`, `na verdade`, `miscount`, `wrong count`), you must cite the tool
output that supersedes the prior claim (command + relevant line). Do not
silently rewrite the number.

## Quick checklist

1. About to say N tests / files / % / scenarios? → run a tool first
2. Tool output differs from what you said? → correct and cite the tool
3. No tool available? → say you have not measured yet; do not invent N
